= <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> Congress

The victory of moderates within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> has not entirely stopped the party’s rightward shift since its electoral defeat years ago. The surprise election of Gottfried Trevannon briefly reversed this trend, but the worsening economic crisis has swung the pendulum in favor of the party’s conservatives once again. Additionally, Trevannon's ambivalence on monarchism has sparked controversy, deepening divisions within the party—this time creating a genuine split, unlike the debate over Maine’s article years prior.

While the turmoil from Mallin’s split and the Serannus Plan has subsided, a further rightward shift remains possible, especially as the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> threatens to eclipse them. Trevannon now faces a battle against the party’s <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> elements as he works to modernize the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and secure its democratic future.

- @treviranus: Trevannon manages to secure his and his party's future.
- @westarp: Westmore is restored to his former position.
- @schiele: The mantle is transferred to Martin Tilford and the <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarians</span>.

@treviranus
choose-if: treviranus_trigger and not westarp_trigger and not schiele_trigger
unavailable-subtitle: [? if schiele_trigger: The <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> wing of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span> objects, claiming that it is their turn to lead. ?][? if westarp_trigger: The national conservatives object, claiming that Trevannon's reforms have gone too far. ?]
on-arrival: treviranus_stays = 1; landed_traditionalist -= 3; landed_royalist += 3; landed_dnf += 3; burgher_traditionalist += 4; burgher_gold -= 2; burgher_ddp -= 2; burgher_lvp -= 4; commons_traditionalist += 2; commons_unionist -= 2; faithful_traditionalist += 6; faithful_unionist -= 3; faithful_other -= 3; pro_republic += traditionalist_votes / 2; gold_left += 5; ddp_left += 2.5; lvp_left += 3
face-image: img/portraits/Trevannon.jpg

Surprisingly, Trevannon has survived efforts to replace him with a more conservative figure, securing a mandate to further reform the party—despite opposition from propertied and <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> elites. [? if hugenberg_removed: However, he remains a puppet of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s old guard—figures like Westmore and Hargen—who block any drastic shift toward <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatism</span>. ?]

While some conservative and <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> supporters defect to the <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> and even the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, the party compensates for these losses by attracting <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">bli</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">cans</span> previously alienated by the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>’s monarchist stance. Although monarchism remains in the party’s platform, it has taken a backseat to more pressing issues.

@westarp
view-if: true_christian_democracy
choose-if: westarp_trigger and not treviranus_trigger and not schiele_trigger
unavailable-subtitle: [? if treviranus_trigger and not schiele_trigger: Trevannon is too popular to replace. ?][? if schiele_trigger: The party prefers to elect Tilford, especially since Westmore has already had his turn at the helm. ?]
on-arrival: traditionalist_leader = "Westmore"; landed_traditionalist += 2; landed_dnf -= 2; burgher_traditionalist -= 3; burgher_gold += 2; burgher_ddp += 1; guild_traditionalist += 5; guild_dnf -= 3; guild_royalist -= 2; commons_traditionalist -= 1; commons_royalist += 1; faithful_traditionalist -= 2; faithful_unionist += 2
face-image: img/portraits/Kuno_von_Westarp.jpg

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s shift toward <span style="color: #0087DC;">Tory Democracy</span> and <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">blic</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">anism</span> has stalled with the re-election of Kuno von Westmore as party leader, promoted from his role as chairman of the Assembly delegation. Experienced with managing internal dissent, Westmore avoids drastic changes to prevent a party split, frustrating the party’s more <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> backers, who had hoped his election would return the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> to its previous course.

While some <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">bli</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">can</span> voters drawn to Trevannon shift back toward propertied parties, Westmore’s more conservative leadership helps reclaim voters from Mallin’s <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span>. However, he opposes active reconciliation with Mallin and his party.

@schiele
choose-if: schiele_trigger
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> wing isn't too displeased with Trevannon.
on-arrival: traditionalist_leader = "Tilford"; landed_traditionalist += 8; landed_royalist -= 4; landed_dnf -= 4; landed_traditionalist += landed_other; landed_other = landed_other*0.2; burgher_traditionalist -= 4; burgher_royalist += 4; commons_traditionalist -= 2; commons_royalist += 2; faithful_traditionalist += 5; faithful_other -= 2; faithful_unionist -= 3; unionist_relation -= 4; traditionalist_r += other_r*0.3; other_r = other_r*0.7
face-image: img/portraits/schiele.jpg

[? if land_reform >= 1 : Due to the land reform policies enacted by our[? if not marcher_in_government:&nbsp;previous?] government, the <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> conservative elites have made it their strongest effort to rally the Commonwealth right against them. This involves orchestrating a leadership change within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, the primary political home of <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> conservatism. Trevannon has been ousted in a vote of no confidence, in favor of the president of the Landed League, Martin Tilford. By electing the most influential figure in the agricultural community, they aim to safeguard the role of organized agriculture in the Commonwealth, viewing Trevannon as too aligned with middle class interests. ?][? if landed_marcher_normalized >= 30 and land_reform == 0 : With the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> making significant inroads among rural voters, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and its <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> elites have ousted Trevannon in a vote of no confidence, to elect Martin Tilford, the president of the Landed League. They believe Tilford, the most influential figure in the agricultural community, can halt this shift and preserve the longstanding alliance between agriculture and Commonwealth conservatism, seeing Trevannon as too aligned with middle-class interests. ?][? if landed_royalist_normalized >= landed_traditionalist_normalized and landed_marcher_normalized < 30 and land_reform == 0 : Due to the significant inroads made by the insurgent <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> among their primary rural voter base, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and its <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> elites have ousted Trevannon in a vote of no confidence, to elect Martin Tilford, president of the Landed League. They believe Tilford, the most influential figure in the agricultural community, can halt this shift and preserve the longstanding alliance between agriculture and Commonwealth conservatism, seeing Trevannon as too aligned with middle-class interests. ?]

Tilford’s election has led to the merger of the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> into the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, strengthening its hold on the countryside and uniting the Landed League in lobbying for <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> interests. This consolidation has given rise to the renewal of the <span style="color: #385A38;">Green Front</span>, an umbrella group of the Landed League, peasant unions, and some Faithful and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]-affiliated agricultural organizations.
